            <ArticleTitle>New-onset headache in an adolescent with MASS syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>177-80; discussion 180-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 15-year-old girl with the &quot;MASS&quot; phenotype (meeting several of the minor criteria for Marfan syndrome) presents with a new onset low-pressure postural headache. Clinical features and magnetic resonance imaging suggested intracranial hypotension, which was confirmed with lumbar puncture. The pathophysiology and treatment of spontaneous intracranial hypotension are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
